<title>FRANCE: FRENCH ELECTION - Final share of seats.</title>
<headline>FRENCH ELECTION - Final share of seats.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the final count of seats in the decisive second round of France's election for the 577-seat National Assembly, held on Sunday, according to the Interior Ministry.</p>
<p>A total of 289 seats is required for an absolute majority.</p>
<p>The table shows the number of seats each party held in the outgoing parliament, followed by the share of seats in the new parliament.</p>
<p> SEATS - FINAL COUNT	  Outgoing   Won</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Extreme-left			0	  0</p>
<p> Communist party		  24	 38</p>
<p> Socialist party		  57	240</p>
<p> PRS*				  5	 12</p>
<p> Other left			 13	 21</p>
<p> Ecologists			  0	  7</p>
<p> Independents			0	  1</p>
<p> RPR**			     246	135</p>
<p> UDF***			    203	108</p>
<p> Other right			29	 14</p>
<p> National Front		    0	  1</p>
<p> Extreme-right		     0	  0</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> TOTAL			     577	577</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Total electorate: 38,487,205    Turnout:    71.07 percent</p>
<p> Votes cast:	 27,353,998    Abstention: 28.92 percent</p>
<p> Valid votes:	25,626,329</p>
<p>*   Radical Socialist Party (centre-left)</p>
<p>**  Rally for the Republic (Gaullists, outgoing coalition)</p>
<p>*** Union for French Democracy (centre-right, outgoing coalition)</p>
